class=\"italic\">some</span>, can be used with both count and non-count nouns. You use <span class=\"italic\">any</span> in negative statements and in questions for both count and non-count nouns.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Many</span> is only used with count nouns.   <span class=\"italic\">Much</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">a little</span> are only used with non-count nouns.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Quantifiers</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Count Nouns </span> <br/>teaspoon, cup\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All<br /> Most<br />  Many<br />  Some<br />  Any<br />  A few<br />  A lot of<br />  A couple of<br />  No\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Non-Count Nouns </span> <br/>water, meat\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All <br /> Some <br /> Any <br /> A little <br /> Much <br /> No\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Not all spices are useful. (Non-Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't use much butter.  (Non-Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you give me a little orange juice?  (Non-Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many people here shop at the market.  (Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Some pizzas have pepperoni.   (Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Put some water in the pot.  (Non-Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Is there any fresh juice? (Count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you have any lemons?  (Count)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to focus on  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to concentrate on; to put an emphasis on ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This morning, our show is going to focus on how to make a variety of delicious soups.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when you listen to a cooking show.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gourmet   ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "food that is high quality, well prepared and/or exotic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love gourmet food! It's delicious!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chef  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who cooks as a profession ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  My compliments to the chef. The meal is excellent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "delicious  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "tasty, very good", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This soup is delicious!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "salt   ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a white crystal you add to food to increase the flavor ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Did you add salt to the soup?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pepper ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a strong spice, often served with salt ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The soup has a bit of pepper.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "soup stock  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the liquid you use as a base for soup", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to prepare the soup stock first.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reduce ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something smaller; to decrease something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Bring the soup to a boil and then reduce the heat. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wonderful  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "excellent; amazing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This soup is wonderful!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bay leaf ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the leaf of the bay tree used in cooking to add flavor ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Add 6-8 cups of water and a lot of bay leaves to add flavor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a good recipe you know or find a recipe online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of 5 - 10 ingredients.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For each ingredient, use a quantifier like <span class=\"italic\">a few</span>, <span class=\"italic\">many</span>, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For non-count nouns, choose a count word you can measure, like <span class=\"italic\">a teaspoon of ...</span>",